XL, stats, luck?  Do you have intrinsic telepathy yet?

In the long run, GDSM would round up your current kit nicely, and I
agree that replacing that mithril-coat with *DSM is a priority if
you'd like to cast spells, and it'll also weigh less.  I think that's
what I'd go for.

I'd also wear the shield even if it hurts your spellcasting.  +3 is
nothing to scoff at, even if it wasn't reflection, and the fact that
it is lets you free up the amulet slot for something else.  You can
always take it off for spellcasting when it's safe enough, especially
if you have a backup reflection source.

I assume you're lugging around Excalibur for the searching intrinsic?
You may want to consider making it your main weapon, especially if you
got it as a gift; it might do better damage than your unihorn even at
unskilled, and should definitely do so at basic.  And it only uses one
hand.  (Also, the searching doesn't work unless you keep it wielded.)

If you don't have a BoH yet, you might want to stash Werebane for now;
silver-haters aren't that common in the early game anyway.  Ditto for
the helm and the mace if you're not actually using them.

Also, if you're not wearing the helm, I'd suggest getting some
alternative headgear.  An elven leather helm would be a good choice.

